    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Malpractice:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " a successful lawsuit requires proof that care was below the ordinary standard of care that similar health care professionals would provide under similar circumstances, that a professional relationship existed with the injured party, and that the patient was harmed because of the deviation from the standard of care."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Defensive medicine:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ordering tests that are not clearly medically necessary to avoid lawsuits exposes patients to risks and expenses not justified by the medical benefit; it is not required by law, may not protect against lawsuits, and is generally considered excessive and inappropriate."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Best defense:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " providing excellent health care and building close, trusting, collaborative relationships with patients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Licensing:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " in the United States, all health care professionals must have a state license to practice, and patients can complain to the state licensing board instead of or in addition to bringing a lawsuit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Board discipline:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " if warranted, reprimand, fine, license suspension or license revocation."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
